description: Explicit grants and RLS on every new public table
alwaysApply: true
---

# New public tables

Every migration that creates a table in public MUST, in the same migration: enable RLS + add policies, and add explicit grants - service_role always (select, insert, update, delete); authenticated only what the feature needs; anon only if logged-out visitors must read it. Never rely on automatic grants (Supabase stopped them Oct 30, 2026).

```sql
alter table public.example enable row level security;

create policy example_owner_read on public.example
  for select to authenticated
  using (profile_id = auth.uid());

grant select, insert, update, delete on public.example to service_role;
grant select on public.example to authenticated;
-- grant select on public.example to anon;  -- only if logged-out visitors must read it
```
